# === Generated experiment data + historical archive (large) ===
**/data/
**/eda/eval/
archive/
# meetings/archive/ is NOT that kind of archive — it holds the tracked records of what the
# supervisors were actually shown (PDFs + email drafts; the .pptx stay ignored by the later *.pptx rule).
# Both negations are needed: the dir must be un-excluded before files inside it can be.
!meetings/archive/
!meetings/archive/**
# papers/archive/ likewise: retired drafts stay tracked (their .tex/.bib/NUMBERS.md/figures/tables).
!papers/archive/
!papers/archive/**
# Sentence-embedding caches (these .npy files are ~139 MB each — over GitHub's limit)
**/emb_cache_words/
*.npy
# exp3 pref completion-embedding cache (~23 MB .pkl; regenerable)
**/.emb_cache/
# exp3 EDA parquet cache (scores_long / behavior_by_iter; regenerable, content-keyed)
**/eda/.eda_cache/

# === Model weights / training artifacts / logs ===
*.safetensors
*.bin
*.pt
*.ckpt
*.gguf
**/runs/
**/checkpoints/
**/outputs/
wandb/

# === Meeting decks / local presentation artifacts ===
*.pptx

